<title>USA: Federated Investors poised to manage six funds.</title>
<headline>Federated Investors poised to manage six funds.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federated Investors said Tuesday it had signed an agreement in principle with ARM Financial Group Inc to manage six retail mutual funds with about $230 million in assets.</p>
<p>Federated, one of the country's largest investment management and financial services companies, did not disclose the terms of the agreement but said it had yet to be approved by the shareholders of the State Bond Group of Funds, under whose name the funds operate.</p>
<p>ARM is a financial services company based in Louisville, Kentucky.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
